$ rust-mutants report --help
Read back a stored run report

Usage: rust-mutants report [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Whether to paint the output. `auto` paints a terminal that has not set `NO_COLOR`

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a terminal that has not asked to go without
          - always: Always
          - never:  Never
          
          [default: auto]

      --root <DIR>
          The workspace root. Defaults to the working directory

      --cargo <PATH>
          Run this cargo, by path, rather than the one found on the `PATH`; its rustc is the one
          beside it

      --run <ID>
          The run, by its identity. Defaults to the newest

      --format <FORMAT>
          How to write it

          Possible values:
          - lines:    The lines a person reads
          - json:     The stored `rust-mutants/run-report` document, verbatim
          - html:     One self-contained HTML page
          - stryker:  The mutation testing report every Stryker reader understands
          - junit:    The JUnit XML a continuous integration server already reads
          - sarif:    The findings as SARIF 2.1.0, for a code scanning view
          - markdown: The summary a person puts in a pull request
          
          [default: lines]

      --output <FILE>
          Write it here rather than to standard output

      --tui
          Read it at the terminal instead of writing it

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

$ rust-mutants cache --help
Say what the engine left in the temporary directory, and remove what no run still owns

Usage: rust-mutants cache [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Whether to paint the output. `auto` paints a terminal that has not set `NO_COLOR`

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a terminal that has not asked to go without
          - always: Always
          - never:  Never
          
          [default: auto]

      --root <DIR>
          The workspace root, whose report directory holds the ledger of what was kept

      --cargo <PATH>
          Run this cargo, by path, rather than the one found on the `PATH`; its rustc is the one
          beside it

      --gc
          Remove every abandoned snapshot, and the build caches no run can look up again

      --all
          With `--gc`, remove every build cache no live run has locked, not only the unowned ones

      --kept
          With `--gc`, remove the directories a run was asked to keep, too

      --clear-outcomes
          Empty the store of what earlier runs established, and say how much was in it

      --cache-dir <DIR>
          Read and write the store under this directory rather than the user's cache directory

      --export <FILE>
          Write every record of the store to this file, each carrying what it was keyed on, for
          another checkout or a CI job to import

      --import <FILE>
          File every record of an exported store under the key its own inputs name, refusing one
          keyed under another release's versions

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

